# This project is deliberately plain Verilog-2001, not SystemVerilog, so it reads
# like the textbook and elaborates in any tool.  Every rule disabled here exists
# only to push code toward SystemVerilog idioms.

# `localparam int OP_ADD` -- typed parameters are SystemVerilog.
-explicit-parameter-storage-type
# `always_comb` -- SystemVerilog.  `always @(*)` is the Verilog-2001 spelling.
-always-comb
# `reg x [N]` -- the compact unpacked-array form is SystemVerilog.
-unpacked-dimensions-range-ordering
# `function automatic` / `task automatic` -- lifetimes are SystemVerilog.
-explicit-function-lifetime
-explicit-task-lifetime
# `$urandom` is SystemVerilog.  `$random(seed)` is Verilog-2001 and, unlike
# $urandom, takes an explicit seed -- which is what makes runs reproducible.
-invalid-system-task-function
# `$value$plusargs` is for plusargs that carry a value.  +dump is a bare flag,
# so `$test$plusargs` is the correct call.
-plusarg-assignment
# The opcode and flag tables in the header comments are wider than 100 columns.
-line-length
# Wants CamelCase localparams (`OpAdd`).  SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE is the near
# universal Verilog convention for constants, and it is what every ALU
# reference you would compare this against uses.
-parameter-name-style
